                <pb facs="0718" n="582" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg582"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.79611 Pan American Airways, Inc./638</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-08-30">August 30, 1929</date>.<lb/>[Received September
                        10.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1638</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith copy
                    and translation of an agreement signed by the local representative of the Pan
                    American Airways, Incorporated, and the Director of Posts of Costa Rica,<anchor
                        n="34" xml:id="d409-f1"/> setting forth the conditions under which air mail
                    service is to be inaugurated, and establishing postal rates for this service.
                    This agreement supplements the contract of the Pan American Airways,
                    Incorporated, which was recently approved by the Costa Rican Congress.</p>
                <p>It will be noted that the agreement is entered into upon the condition that the
                    Company may request an interpretation of Article 17 of the Contract.</p>
                <p>Under this agreement, the Pan American Airways, Incorporated, can begin
                    operations immediately and will enjoy all the rights granted by the contract
                    until such time as the Company may find it advisable to request an
                    interpretation of Article 17, to which it has raised some objections.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Roy T. Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
